1. **A DC-DC converter comprising:**

a substrate;

a transformer including a primary winding and a secondary winding;

a primary-side circuit disposed on the substrate and electrically coupled to the primary winding, the primary-side circuit being configured to receive a DC input and drive the primary winding;

a secondary-side circuit disposed on the substrate and electrically coupled to the secondary winding, the secondary-side circuit being configured to produce a DC output;

one or more inter-circuit connections extending between the primary-side circuit and the secondary-side circuit, each of the one or more inter-circuit connections providing DC isolation between the primary-side circuit and the secondary-side circuit; and

a secondary-side choke coil electrically coupled to the secondary-side circuit and supported above a selected portion of the secondary-side circuit such that the secondary-side choke coil overlaps the selected portion when viewed in a direction normal to a major surface of the substrate.
